await write('docs/methodology.html',shell('Methodology',`<section class="prose"><div class="eyebrow">TRUST AND GOVERNANCE</div><h1>Methodology</h1><h2>Classification model</h2><p>Organizations are classified independently across executive roles, provider types, community formats, event formats, intelligence types, resources, executive needs, topics, and geographies. A multi-category organization retains one canonical entity record.</p><h2>Controlled vocabulary</h2><p>Every semantic term has a stable ID and neutral definition. Closely related phrases map to one canonical concept unless they represent a material distinction.</p><h2>Evidence requirement</h2><p>Entity associations require reasonable evidence from official organization, event, research, regulatory, government, or reputable third-party sources. A passing keyword mention is insufficient.</p><h2>Indexability gate</h2><p>Arbitrary filter combinations remain application state. A canonical page is created only when it has stable intent, enough substantive entities, distinct analysis, and durable value.</p><h2>Commercial neutrality</h2><p>Inclusion does not constitute endorsement. Commercial relationships do not influence inclusion, ranking, scoring, descriptions, or category placement.</p><h2>Versioning</h2><p>Schema and dataset versions are published in exports. Stable IDs do not change without a documented migration.</p></section>`));
